.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
.Dd November 8, 2026
.Dt PQSCAN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pqscan
.Nd find cryptography that quantum computers will break
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Ar path ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
finds RSA, ECDSA, EdDSA, ECDH, DH and DSA, which Shor's algorithm breaks, and
classically
weak algorithms such as MD5, SHA-1, DES and RC4, in C and C++ source, TLS and
SSH
configuration, certificates and keys, and 64-bit ELF binaries.
For each finding it reports where it is, the algorithm and key size, a risk
level and a
migration priority.
.Pp
Each
.Ar path
is a file or a directory.
Directories are walked recursively, and symbolic links inside them are skipped.
Files are chosen by name, except ELF files, which are recognized by their first
four bytes:
.Bl -tag -width "Certificates and keys"
.It C and C++ source
.Pa .c , .h , .cpp , .hpp , .cc , .cxx , .C , .hh , .hxx , .ipp , .inl
and
.Pa .tcc .
Files are parsed with Tree-sitter, so comments, unrelated strings and
declarations are not
reported.
Constants defined in the same file are followed to find key sizes and algorithm
names.
A value that cannot be proven is reported as
.Ql unknown .
.It Configuration
.Pa .conf , .cnf , sshd_config , ssh_config , .htaccess ,
and any file in a
.Pa sites-available
or
.Pa sites-enabled
directory.
The algorithm lists of OpenSSL, nginx, Apache and OpenSSH settings are read.
.It Certificates and keys
.Pa .pem , .crt , .cer , .der , .key
and
.Pa .csr ,
in PEM or DER, decoded with OpenSSL's libcrypto.
A certificate also reports the algorithm that signed it and when it expires.
.Nm
never asks for a passphrase.
.It ELF binaries
64-bit executables, shared libraries and object files, in either byte order.
Function symbols, defined or imported, are matched against the rules.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
never executes or loads what it scans.
.Ss Risk levels
Each finding has the most severe level that applies, here from the least to the
most severe:
.Bl -tag -width CLASSICALLY_WEAK
.It Cm OK
AES-256, SHA-256 and stronger, ML-KEM, ML-DSA, SLH-DSA.
.It Cm REVIEW
AES-128 and other symmetric algorithms that Grover's algorithm weakens.
.It Cm QUANTUM_VULNERABLE
RSA, ECDSA, EdDSA, ECDH, DH and DSA, which must migrate to ML-KEM or ML-DSA.
.It Cm CLASSICALLY_WEAK
MD5, SHA-1, DES, 3DES, RC4, and RSA, DSA or DH keys under 2048 bits, which are
unsafe today.
.El
.Ss Priorities
Every finding gets a priority from 0 to 100, and reports list the most urgent
first.
.Cm CLASSICALLY_WEAK
is 100,
.Cm REVIEW
is 10 and
.Cm OK
is 0.
A
.Cm QUANTUM_VULNERABLE
finding scores from 50 to 99, from the NIST IR 8547 dates, which deprecate
these algorithms
after 2030 and disallow them after 2035, and from Mosca's theorem: data that
must stay secret
for X years, in code that takes Y years to migrate, is exposed when X + Y > Q,
where Q is the
number of years until a quantum computer arrives.
X, Y and the quantum year come from the project file, see
.Sx FILES .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl i , Fl -ignore Ar pattern
Skip the paths matching the glob
.Ar pattern ,
tried on the file name, on the path, and on the path relative to the
.Ar path
argument.
Can be repeated.
.Pa .git
is always skipped.
.It Fl r , Fl -rules Ar file
Use the rules in the JSON
.Ar file
instead of the built-in ones.
.It Fl -project Ar file
Read how long data must stay secret from this project file.
The default is
.Pa .pqscan.json
in the current directory, if there is one.
.It Fl -as-of Ar year
Score priorities as if it were
.Ar year ,
from 1970 to 9999.
The default is the current year, in UTC.
.It Fl -diff Ar file
Report only the findings that the baseline
.Ar file
does not accept.
Entries that no finding used are counted on the standard error.
.It Fl -write-baseline Ar file
Write a baseline that accepts every finding to
.Ar file ,
and report as usual.
Cannot be combined with
.Fl -diff .
.It Fl f , Fl -format Ar format
Write the report as
.Cm text ,
the default,
.Cm json ,
.Cm cbom ,
a CycloneDX 1.6 cryptography bill of materials, or
.Cm sarif ,
SARIF 2.1.0 for code scanning services.
.It Fl -fail-on Ar level
The lowest risk level that makes
.Nm
exit 1:
.Cm OK ,
.Cm REVIEW ,
.Cm QUANTUM_VULNERABLE
or
.Cm CLASSICALLY_WEAK .
The default is
.Cm REVIEW .
Every finding is still reported.
.It Fl -max-time Ar seconds
Start on no new file after this many seconds.
The default is 3600.
Files left over are skipped, which makes the scan incomplete.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show the help and exit.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Show the version and exit.
.El
.Sh OUTPUT
The report goes to the standard output, and warnings go to the standard error.
The text report has one line per finding, most urgent first, followed by a
count:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
src/keys.c:51: RSA-1024 (CLASSICALLY_WEAK, priority 100)
src/keys.c:42: RSA-2048 (QUANTUM_VULNERABLE, priority 51)
tls/server.pem:1: RSA-2048 (QUANTUM_VULNERABLE, priority 51, expires 2031-05-01)
3 findings: 1 CLASSICALLY_WEAK, 2 QUANTUM_VULNERABLE
.Ed
.Pp
A clean scan prints nothing.
A finding about a whole file, such as a DER certificate or a binary, has no
line number.
Control characters, bidirectional marks and invalid UTF-8 in file names are
printed as
.Ql \exNN .
.Pp
The same files, rules, project file and
.Fl -as-of
year always give the same bytes: reports hold no timestamp and no random
identifier.
.Pp
A file that cannot be analyzed is skipped with a warning, and the scan is then
incomplete.
That covers paths that cannot be read, files over 64 MiB, source and
configuration files with
a NUL byte, source files that take more than 30 seconds to parse, encrypted
PKCS#8 keys,
certificates and keys that cannot be decoded, and ELF files that are 32-bit,
damaged or have
no symbol table.
Every report format says when a scan is incomplete.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Nm
reads no environment variable.
OpenSSL is started without reading
.Ev OPENSSL_CONF ,
so a scan never depends on the environment.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa .pqscan.json
The project file, read from the current directory unless
.Fl -project
names another.
It sets the quantum year and, for the whole project or per component, how many
years data must
stay secret and how many the migration takes.
It changes only priorities and their order, never which findings are reported
or the exit
status.
.It Pa .pqscan-baseline.json
The usual name of a baseline, written by
.Fl -write-baseline
and read by
.Fl -diff .
An entry accepts a finding by its path, algorithm, symbol, primitive and key
size, not its
line, so editing code above a finding does not make it new.
.It Pa share/pqscan/default.json
Under the installation prefix, a copy of the built-in rules, to start a rules
file for
.Fl -rules
from.
.El
.Pp
Each of these files is JSON with a
.Ql schema_version ,
and
.Nm
refuses a whole file over any mistake, such as an unknown field.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
No findings at or above the
.Fl -fail-on
level, and everything in scope was analyzed.
.It 1
Findings at or above the
.Fl -fail-on
level, even if the scan was incomplete.
With
.Fl -diff ,
only new findings count, and with
.Fl -write-baseline ,
none do.
.It 2
Usage error, such as a path that does not exist or a rules, project or baseline
file that is
not valid.
.It 3
Internal error, such as a report that cannot be written.
.It 4
No findings at or above the
.Fl -fail-on
level, but something in scope could not be analyzed.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Scan a project, skipping vendored code:
.Pp
.Dl $ pqscan --ignore third_party \&.
.Pp
Write a CycloneDX inventory of the cryptography in use:
.Pp
.Dl $ pqscan --format cbom \&. > cbom.json
.Pp
Accept the findings a project has today, then fail only on new ones:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pqscan --write-baseline .pqscan-baseline.json .
$ pqscan --diff .pqscan-baseline.json .
.Ed
.Pp
Fail only on what is broken today, but report everything:
.Pp
.Dl $ pqscan --fail-on CLASSICALLY_WEAK \&.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr ssh_config 5 ,
.Xr sshd_config 5
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/HarenaFiantso/pqscan
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%A Dustin Moody et al.
.%T Transition to Post-Quantum Cryptography Standards
.%R NIST IR 8547
.%I National Institute of Standards and Technology
.%D 2024
.Re
.Pp
Reports follow CycloneDX 1.6 and SARIF 2.1.0.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Fiantso Harena
.Sh CAVEATS
Exit status 0 does not prove that code is free of vulnerable cryptography.
.Nm
only recognizes the names in its rules, in the kinds of files listed above.
.Pp
Constants are only followed inside one file.
Configuration aliases such as
.Ql DEFAULT
or
.Ql HIGH
are not expanded, since their meaning depends on the OpenSSL that reads them.
A stripped, statically linked binary keeps no symbol table, so it cannot be
analyzed, and
32-bit ELF files and
.Pa .a
archives are not read.
